மாறு","parts":[{"text":"மாறு","lemma":"மாறு","gloss":"because of/instead"}],"gloss":"because of"},{"surface":"கொல்","parts":[{"text":"கொல்","lemma":"கொல்","gloss":"interrogative particle"}],"gloss":"is it?"},{"surface":"விசி","parts":[{"text":"விசி","lemma":"விசி","gloss":"tighten"}],"gloss":"tight"},{"surface":"பிணி","parts":[{"text":"பிணி","lemma":"பிணி","gloss":"binding"}],"gloss":"binding"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கூடு","parts":[{"text":"கூடு","lemma":"கூடு","gloss":"frame/assembly"}],"gloss":"frame"},{"surface":"கொள்","parts":[{"text":"கொள்","lemma":"கொள்","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"having"},{"surface":"இன்னியம்","parts":[{"text":"இன்னியம்","lemma":"இன்னியம்","gloss":"sweet instruments"}],"gloss":"sweet instruments","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கறங்க","parts":[{"text":"கறங்கு","lemma":"கறங்கு","gloss":"sound"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to sound"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆடலும்","parts":[{"text":"ஆடல்","lemma":"ஆடல்","gloss":"dancing"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"dancing and"},{"surface":"ஒல்லார்","parts":[{"text":"ஒல்","lemma":"ஒல்","gloss":"agree/do"},{"text":"ஆர்","lemma":"ஆர்","gloss":"negative third person plural suffix"}],"gloss":"they do not do"},{"surface":"தம்","parts":[{"text":"தம்","lemma":"தம்","gloss":"their"}],"gloss":"their"},{"surface":"பாடலும்","parts":[{"text":"பாடல்","lemma":"பாடல்","gloss":"singing"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"singing and"},{"surface":"மறந்தே","parts":[{"text":"மறந்தே","lemma":"மறந்தே","gloss":"having forgotten indeed"}],"gloss":"having forgotten indeed","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"Lord of the rain-adorned hill, daily / giving elephant adorned with ornaments to those who ask, / possessing forearms of beauty with glowing gold ornaments, / unceasing in slaying war, Āthaṉ Ōri, / to see his rain-like generous gifts, greatly / went indeed our dancers' troupe. / Not blossoming in cold water, gem-set blue lilies, / strung with white fiber, chaplets and ornaments, / with a herd of elephants they received, and departing, / is it because they became free from hunger? / While tightly bound, framed sweet instruments sound, / they do not even dance, having forgotten their songs!","translation":"Our troupe of dancers went with great eagerness to witness the rain-like generosity of Āthaṉ Ōri, the lord of the rain-swept hills, who daily gives ornament-adorned elephants to those who ask, and whose strong forearms are clasped with glowing gold ornaments, unceasing in victorious war. Having received golden blue-lily chaplets set with sapphires—flowers that never blossomed in cold water—strung on fine white fiber, along with other ornaments and a whole herd of elephants, they departed. Is it because they are now completely free from hunger? Though their tightly-bound, well-crafted sweet instruments sound, they no longer care to dance, having forgotten even their songs!","modern":"மழை மேகங்கள் சூழ்ந்த மலையின் தலைவனும், இரப்பவர்க்கு நாள்தோறும் அணிகலன்கள் அணிந்த யானைகளைக் கொடையாக வழங்குபவனும், ஒளிவீசும் பொன்னணிகலன்கள் பொருந்திய அழகிய முன்கைகளை உடையவனும், வெல்லும் போரில் சளைக்காதவனுமாகிய ஆதன் ஓரியின் மழை போன்ற கொடைத்தன்மையைக் காண்பதற்காக எமது கூத்தர் சுற்றம் சென்றது. குளிர்ந்த நீரில் மலராத, நீலமணிகள் பதிக்கப்பட்ட குவளை மலர் போன்ற பொன் மாலைகளையும், பிற அணிகலன்களையும், யானைக் கூட்டங்களையும் அவர்கள் பரிசாகப் பெற்றுத் திரும்பினர். பசி நீங்கிய காரணத்தினாலோ என்னவோ, இறுக்கமாகக் கட்டப்பட்ட இசைக்கருவிகள் ஒலித்தபோதும், அவர்கள் ஆடவும் இல்லை; தங்கள் பாடல்களையும் மறந்துவிட்டனர்.","explanation":"The poet Vaṇparaṇar praises the chieftain Valvil Ōri (Āthaṉ Ōri) for his extraordinary generosity. The poet describes how his troupe of bards and dancers visited Ōri and were showered with such immense wealth, including golden ornaments, sapphire-studded lotus garlands, and herds of elephants, that they became completely free from poverty. The poem ends with a beautiful touch of irony: usually, artists perform to earn their livelihood, but Ōri's gifts were so overwhelming that they no longer feel the pinch of hunger. Consequently, they have forgotten their very art of singing and dancing, even when their instruments are played. The imagery of the rain-swept hills reflects the fertile, generous nature of the patron, comparing his gifts to the unceasing rain.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.2],[1.2,1.3],[1.3,1.6],[1.6,2.6],[2.6,2.6],[2.6,3.2],[3.2,3.9],[3.9,5.0],[5.0,5.3],[5.3,6.2],[6.2,6.2],[6.2,6.6],[6.6,7.8],[7.8,7.8],[7.8,8.2],[8.2,8.7],[8.7,9.46],[9.46,9.64],[9.64,9.83],[9.83,10.4],[10.4,12.1],[12.1,12.4],[12.4,12.5],[12.5,13.12],[13.12,13.5],[13.5,14.5],[14.5,14.8],[14.8,15.1],[15.1,15.4],[15.4,16.19],[16.19,16.5],[16.5,17.3],[17.3,17.7],[18.48,19.08],[19.08,19.48],[19.48,19.58],[19.58,19.98],[19.98,20.73],[20.88,21.28],[21.28,21.58],[21.58,22.18],[22.18,23.28],[23.28,23.38],[23.38,23.88],[23.88,24.98],[24.98,25.08],[25.08,25.58],[25.58,25.88],[25.88,26.28]],"female":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,1.3],[1.3,1.4],[1.4,1.7],[1.7,2.9],[2.9,2.9],[2.9,3.5],[3.5,4.3],[4.3,5.6],[5.6,5.9],[5.9,6.7],[6.7,6.8],[6.8,7.3],[7.3,8.4],[8.4,8.5],[8.5,8.9],[8.9,9.3],[9.3,10.59],[10.59,10.91],[10.91,11.23],[11.23,12.2],[12.2,13.0],[13.0,13.3],[13.3,13.4],[13.4,14.29],[14.29,14.7],[14.7,15.8],[15.8,16.1],[16.1,16.5],[16.5,16.8],[17.04,17.77],[17.77,18.5],[18.5,19.2],[19.2,19.7],[20.48,21.18],[21.18,21.68],[21.68,21.88],[21.88,22.38],[22.38,23.38],[23.78,24.34],[24.34,24.34],[24.34,25.38],[25.38,26.48],[26.48,26.58],[26.58,27.18],[27.18,28.38],[28.38,28.48],[28.48,28.98],[28.98,29.18],[29.18,29.78]]}}